                    "details": "The heavier Bi-Turbo front end loads the front suspension harder than the earlier naturally aspirated version, so control arm bushings, ball joints, and drop links wear steadily with mileage. Early symptoms usually include light knocking over rough roads, vague steering response, and uneven front tyre wear."
