                        "critical": true,
                        "details": "The upper center of the engine bay is the key inspection point for the M278-powered facelift CLS 550’s most expensive support-system issues, including charge-air leaks, PCV-related problems, ignition access, upper oil seepage, and turbo-adjacent heat stress. Many of the engine’s costly problems start here gradually, so this is the most important hotspot for a serious condition check."
