                            "details": "The rear multi-link suspension has to manage much greater torque and tyre load than the regular CLS range, so worn arm bushings, bearing noise, and reduced body control appear more clearly as the car ages. This usually shows up as inner-edge tyre wear, humming at speed, or a less settled rear axle during aggressive direction changes."
