                        "oilSpecification": "9.0L 0W-40 or 5W-40 Fully Synthetic (MB 229.5 / AMG-approved specification. Correct oil and short intervals are critical because turbocharger heat load, valvetrain stability, and internal cleanliness all depend on them.)",
                        "commonIssues": [
                          "Cooling-system stress is one of the central ownership themes on the M157 because the Bi-Turbo AMG V8 generates substantial sustained heat. Thermostat aging, coolant-system weakness, and heat-sensitive ancillary wear often begin gradually before turning into expensive reliability problems.",
                          "Charge-air and boost-system leaks matter because this engine can still feel brutally fast while already losing precision and consistency. Aging hoses, seals, and pressure-side components can reduce response quality and thermal efficiency before a warning light forces attention.",
                          "Ignition wear becomes highly visible under AMG load because this drivetrain is unforgiving of tired spark plugs and weak coils. Misfire under hard acceleration, inconsistent torque delivery, and roughness under boost are common early warning signs.",
                          "Oil seepage from upper-engine areas, breather-related components, and turbo-adjacent seals is not unusual as mileage and heat cycles accumulate. These leaks rarely remain isolated and quickly complicate diagnosis in an already crowded and hot engine bay.",
                          "Direct-injection carbon buildup is a long-term concern rather than a sudden disaster, but it changes how the engine behaves over time. Throttle sharpness, idle quality, and smoothness can all drift away from the factory AMG feel as deposits build.",
                          "PCV and crankcase-ventilation issues can contribute to whistle noises, idle irregularity, oil-control problems, and mixture-related drivability faults. These problems often overlap with other support-system issues and make proper diagnosis more demanding.",
                          "Turbo-related heat management remains a major ownership factor even when the turbochargers themselves are not yet failing. Repeated hot operation, overdue oil changes, and neglected cooling components often damage surrounding support hardware first.",
                          "Transmission and drivetrain neglect are especially important here because the AMG MCT gearbox and 4MATIC system are central to the S-model’s character. When service history is poor, the whole car loses sharpness, launch consistency, and mechanical confidence."
                        ],
                        "vulnerabilities": [
                          "This drivetrain is vulnerable to stacked high-cost heat-related and driveline-related faults rather than one universally dominant failure point. A tired example can still feel extremely fast during a short drive while hiding boost leaks, ignition weakness, cooling problems, oil seepage, and AWD-related wear all at once.",
                          "The engine is highly dependent on thermal stability because turbocharging and AMG calibration raise stress across the entire support system. A weak thermostat, aging coolant hardware, or heat-hardened hose can quietly reduce reliability long before a major failure appears.",
                          "Because it is direct injected, electronically complex, and heavily loaded, it is vulnerable to subtle drivability decline. Small airflow errors, sensor faults, and adaptation issues can make the car feel less sharp and less expensive without producing one simple diagnostic clue.",
                          "The M157.981 S-model is also vulnerable to ownership shortcuts, especially extended oil intervals and low-budget tuning on an already tired car. Strong acceleration does not reliably indicate healthy condition on this platform.",
                          "Transmission and AWD condition remain major hidden vulnerabilities because the car’s traction can mask deterioration in shift quality and driveline smoothness for a while. Once both engine and driveline need corrective work together, ownership costs escalate very quickly."
                        ],
