                                "details": "The rear exhaust section is exposed to moisture, vibration, and long-term heat cycling, so clamps, hangers, and the rear silencer area can age faster than expected. Small leaks or deteriorated rubber mounts often begin here and gradually turn into vibration or metallic rattling."
