                                    "x": 0.01,
                                    "y": 0.02,
                                    "z": 0.25,
                                    "critical": true,
                                    "details": "The center of the engine bay is the main inspection point for upper-engine issues, including oil seepage, intake-related faults, ignition access, and cooling-system aging. This is the most important hotspot because many expensive problems begin here gradually rather than as sudden failures."
