                                                    "x": 0.01,
                                                    "y": 0.02,
                                                    "z": 0.25,
                                                    "critical": true,
                                                    "details": "The center of the V6 engine bay is the main inspection point for facelift OM642.853 ownership risks, including oil cooler seal seepage, swirl-flap system faults, injector sealing problems, and the wider emissions burden created by the later SCR / NOx-control hardware. This is the most important hotspot because many expensive facelift OM642 issues begin gradually rather than as sudden failures."
