      "oilSpecification": "Approx. 8.5L 0W-30 or 5W-30 Fully Synthetic MB 229.52 / MB 229.51 low-SAPS oil. Correct oil quality and sensible service intervals are essential because turbocharger durability, timing components, internal cleanliness, and long-term emissions stability all depend on them.",
      "commonIssues": [
        "Ignition-coil and spark-plug condition still matter because even a refined turbocharged inline-six quickly loses smoothness and composure when ignition quality begins to fall away from optimal condition. Small misfires can also add unnecessary catalyst and particulate-filter stress over time.",
        "Charge-air leaks, boost-control problems, or intake-side sealing issues can noticeably reduce the engine’s otherwise rich and immediate mid-range. Because the M256 is so smooth when healthy, even moderate boost-side deterioration is often felt clearly by attentive drivers.",
        "Direct-injection intake carbon buildup remains a long-term issue because fuel no longer washes the intake valves in the traditional way. The problem usually shows up first as slightly rougher idle quality, less crisp response, or a subtle loss of smoothness rather than sudden failure.",
        "Cooling-system stability is important because the engine delivers strong real-world pace and carries more thermal load than its relaxed character suggests. Thermostat drift, ageing pumps, or ignored coolant condition can create a chain of secondary issues if neglected.",
        "The mild-hybrid support layer adds complexity around low-speed refinement, starting behavior, and support-system diagnostics. It improves the overall driving experience when healthy, but when faults appear they can make diagnosis significantly more involved.",
        "PCV and crankcase-ventilation health matter because excess oil vapor accelerates intake contamination and can reduce long-term combustion quality. On a modern turbocharged direct-injection six-cylinder, small ventilation issues often appear first as refinement changes rather than obvious mechanical drama.",
        "Fuel-system cleanliness and injector quality remain important because the M256 depends on precise direct injection to preserve its premium road manners. Poor fuel quality or ageing injector behavior can create a modern kind of roughness that feels out of place in a car of this class.",
        "Transmission servicing still matters because the 9G-Tronic is a major part of what makes the whole drivetrain feel expensive. Shift hesitation, flare, or low-speed harshness can be misread as engine-side drivability issues if gearbox maintenance has been ignored."
      ],
      "vulnerabilities": [
        "The M256.930 is vulnerable to the same broad modern turbocharged direct-injection ownership pattern as other high-end current Mercedes petrol engines, where several smaller condition issues can overlap before one obvious failure appears. A car can still feel fast and smooth while hiding early ignition weakness, intake contamination, minor charge-air leakage, and thermal-management drift together.",
        "This engine remains highly dependent on maintenance quality because the smoothness and strength of the inline-six can hide deterioration better than a harsher four-cylinder would. Long oil intervals, ignored coolant ageing, delayed ignition service, and weak diagnosis usually make later repairs more expensive than necessary.",
        "Because the engine, emissions hardware, transmission logic, and hybrid-assistance system are all closely integrated, the car is especially vulnerable to incomplete diagnosis. Owners who replace parts one symptom at a time often spend much more money than those who evaluate the entire drivetrain condition correctly from the start.",
        "Thermal management remains a secondary vulnerability because the M256.930 is a strong-output turbocharged six-cylinder with real heat load despite its relaxed character. When oil quality, cooling stability, and boost efficiency are all healthy, the engine feels exceptional, but when they are not, the car can quietly drift away from that standard without one dramatic warning sign.",
        "The EQ Boost support layer adds a newer type of ownership risk compared with older Mercedes six-cylinder petrol engines. It does not make the car unreliable by default, but it does mean that smooth operation today does not automatically guarantee inexpensive ownership tomorrow."
      ],
