                  "details": "The center of the engine bay is the main inspection point for the M256.930 drivetrain, including ignition quality, intake contamination, charge-air system integrity, turbo-related ageing, and general upper-engine leaks or heat stress. This is the most important hotspot because many expensive modern turbo six-cylinder issues begin gradually here rather than as one dramatic failure."
