                              "yearRange": "2018-2020",
                              "timingType": "Double overhead camshaft, 4-valve-per-cylinder, chain-driven inline-four timing layout. The UK-spec OM654.920 gives the CLS 220 d a refined long-distance diesel character with good low-end torque, efficient motorway cruising ability, and a calmer overall feel than the petrol six-cylinder versions. In this RHD-oriented market tune, the output is slightly lower than the standard 194 hp version, but the engine still keeps the broad usability and smooth cruising behavior that suit the C257 platform well. This remains a modern common-rail diesel with turbocharging, advanced emissions hardware, and tight software integration. Oil quality, EGR cleanliness, DPF health, AdBlue system behavior, and transmission servicing still matter greatly. A healthy example feels efficient, quiet, and properly premium. A neglected one becomes expensive through emissions and drivability-related overlap rather than one single fault.",
                              "injectionType": "Common-rail direct-injection diesel system with high-pressure fuel delivery, variable-geometry turbocharging, intercooling, and market-specific emissions aftertreatment calibration. The UK-spec OM654.920 depends on precise injector behavior and clean combustion control to preserve the smooth and refined character expected from a diesel CLS. Because it is still a modern low-emissions diesel, fuel quality, injector health, EGR cleanliness, and DPF condition matter just as much as the core engine itself. The slightly altered emissions profile does not change the underlying ownership logic. When healthy, the engine feels strong in the low and mid-range without needing many revs. When fuel, air, or emissions-system quality drifts, the car quickly loses some of its premium character.",
                              "engineLifespan": "280,000 to 450,000 km. The OM654.920 can achieve very good long-term mileage when maintained correctly, because the base diesel concept is well suited to long-distance executive use and operates with strong real-world efficiency. Oil-change discipline, correct low-SAPS oil, fuel-system cleanliness, cooling-system stability, DPF health, and 9G-Tronic servicing all influence long-term ownership quality. Cars used mostly for short trips and cold starts tend to age much worse than regularly driven long-distance examples. The UK-market emissions calibration does not change the strong core durability of the engine, but it does keep diagnosis and software behavior important. The emissions-system layer also means there is more to own than the long block alone. A properly maintained example can remain an excellent high-mileage drivetrain. A neglected one often becomes expensive through stacked emissions and intake-related repair work.",
                              "turboType": "Single variable-geometry turbocharged inline-four diesel engine with intercooling. The turbocharger is a major part of what makes the OM654.920 feel stronger than its modest displacement suggests, because it gives the engine a broad and useful torque curve for everyday driving. The result is a drivetrain that feels relaxed and efficient rather than highly stressed. Boost integrity, charge-air sealing, oil quality, and thermal stability remain important with age. This is a very convincing modern Mercedes diesel when healthy. It still depends on disciplined maintenance to stay that way.",
                              "ecuType": "Modern Mercedes/Bosch-style diesel engine management with common-rail injection control, turbocharger coordination, EGR management, DPF regeneration logic, SCR / AdBlue dosing, and RHD-market emissions calibration strategy. The ECU has to coordinate combustion quality, emissions efficiency, thermal management, and transmission behavior as one system, which is why subtle sensor drift or injector, boost, or emissions issues can affect drivability well before the engine feels obviously unhealthy. Accurate diagnosis matters much more than guesswork. In healthy condition, the drivetrain feels smooth and efficient. In tired condition, it can feel flatter, noisier, and more interrupted than a premium diesel CLS should.",
                              "euroStandard": "Euro 6d-TEMP diesel configuration with DPF, SCR / AdBlue, and market-specific RHD emissions control",
                              "maxPowerStockInternals": "220-240 hp. The OM654.920 has some sensible tuning headroom because the 2.0-liter diesel already has a strong torque-focused factory calibration, but it is also a modern emissions-heavy drivetrain that rewards moderation. A conservative tune can make the car feel fuller in the mid-range, but it only makes sense on examples with stable cooling, healthy DPF and SCR systems, clean intake flow, and strong injector behavior. Aggressive tuning mainly increases thermal and emissions stress. This engine rewards condition-first tuning rather than headline chasing.",
                              "fuelConsumption": {
                                "city": "5.5-6.0 L/100km",
                                "highway": "4.2-4.6 L/100km",
                                "mixed": "4.7-5.2 L/100km",
                                "sporty": "6.2-7.5 L/100km"
                              },
                              "oilSpecification": "Approx. 6.5L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Fully Synthetic MB 229.71 / MB 229.52 low-SAPS oil. Correct oil quality and sensible service intervals are essential because timing components, turbocharger durability, internal cleanliness, and long-term emissions stability all depend on them.",
                              "commonIssues": [
                                "EGR contamination and intake-side soot buildup remain important because a modern low-emissions diesel depends on clean airflow and controlled recirculation to preserve smoothness and efficiency.",
                                "DPF health is strongly influenced by driving pattern because frequent short trips and interrupted regeneration cycles can gradually create backpressure and drivability-related issues.",
                                "AdBlue / SCR system faults, NOx sensor issues, or dosing-system irregularities can create warning lights, limp-mode behavior, and expensive diagnostic work if ignored.",
                                "Charge-air leaks, turbo-control issues, or intake sealing problems can reduce the engine's otherwise broad and useful torque delivery.",
                                "Fuel-system cleanliness and injector quality remain important because the OM654 depends on precise common-rail injection to preserve refinement, efficiency, and emissions stability.",
                                "Cooling-system stability matters because thermostat drift or pump ageing can affect both efficiency and regeneration behavior over time.",
                                "Transmission servicing still matters because the 9G-Tronic is a major part of what makes the whole drivetrain feel refined and premium.",
                                "Glow plug and control-module condition can become relevant with age, especially on cars that see many cold starts or mostly short-distance use."
                              ],
                              "vulnerabilities": [
                                "The UK-spec OM654.920 is vulnerable to the same broad modern diesel ownership pattern as other current premium Euro 6 drivetrains, where several smaller intake, fuel, and emissions issues can overlap before one clear failure appears.",
                                "This engine remains highly dependent on maintenance quality because the smoothness of the drivetrain can hide early deterioration better than older, harsher diesels did.",
                                "Because the engine, DPF, SCR / AdBlue system, sensors, and gearbox logic are closely integrated, incomplete diagnosis remains one of the biggest ownership risks.",
                                "Short-trip use is a meaningful secondary vulnerability because it directly affects soot load, regeneration quality, intake cleanliness, and long-term emissions reliability.",
                                "The market-specific emissions profile is slightly different, but it does not make the drivetrain simpler or cheaper to ignore."
                              ],
