                                  "oilSpecification": "Approx. 6.5L 0W-20 or 5W-30 Fully Synthetic MB 229.71 / MB 229.52 low-SAPS oil. Correct oil quality and sensible service intervals are essential because timing components, turbocharger durability, internal cleanliness, and long-term emissions stability all depend on them.",
                                  "commonIssues": [
                                    "EGR contamination and intake-side soot buildup remain important because a modern high-output diesel depends on clean airflow and controlled recirculation to preserve response and efficiency.",
                                    "DPF health is strongly influenced by driving pattern because frequent short trips and interrupted regeneration cycles can gradually create backpressure and drivability-related issues.",
                                    "AdBlue / SCR system faults, NOx sensor issues, or dosing-system irregularities can create warning lights, limp-mode behavior, and expensive diagnostic work if ignored.",
                                    "Charge-air leaks, turbo-control issues, or intake sealing problems can reduce the engine's otherwise strong and broad torque delivery.",
                                    "Fuel-system cleanliness and injector quality remain important because the OM654 depends on precise common-rail injection to preserve refinement, efficiency, and emissions stability.",
                                    "Cooling-system stability matters because thermostat drift or pump ageing can affect both efficiency and regeneration behavior over time.",
                                    "The 48V mild-hybrid support system adds extra electrical complexity around battery condition, power electronics, and support-system diagnostics.",
                                    "Transmission servicing still matters because the 9G-Tronic is a major part of what makes the whole drivetrain feel refined and quick."
                                  ],
                                  "vulnerabilities": [
                                    "The OM654.820 in CLS 300 d MHEV form is vulnerable to the same broad modern diesel ownership pattern as other current premium Euro 6 drivetrains, where several smaller intake, fuel, boost, electrical-support, and emissions issues can overlap before one clear failure appears.",
                                    "This engine remains highly dependent on maintenance quality because the stronger calibration creates less comfort margin than the softer lower-output versions.",
                                    "Because the engine, turbo system, DPF, SCR / AdBlue system, 48V support hardware, sensors, and gearbox logic are closely integrated, incomplete diagnosis remains one of the biggest ownership risks.",
                                    "Short-trip use is a meaningful secondary vulnerability because it directly affects soot load, regeneration quality, intake cleanliness, and long-term emissions reliability.",
                                    "The stronger factory tune and hybrid support make the car more complete to drive, but they also make neglect more expensive."
                                  ],
